6, 1860],\n  \"window\": [22831, 51631],\n  \"confidence\": 0.60,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_02\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_03\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_07\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_05\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_06\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_10\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_14\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_15\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_16\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"}\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"There is insufficient temporal evidence in the inspected results to confirm a time-respecting cascade from 1006 to 1860 within [22831,51631]. Direct 1006\u21941860 events are absent (step_02). Both nodes do have a small number of events in the window (step_03) and the combined activity is sparsely distributed across subwindows (step_07), but the queries returned only static neighborhood and aggregate counts. Static connectivity and intermediate links exist (1006 neighbors: step_05; 1860 neighbors: step_06; a bridging hub 1680 connects to nodes that are neighbors of 1860: step_10; and 1006 has interactions with its neighbors: steps_14\u201316), which shows plausible static routes. However, without event-level timestamps for the needed intermediate interactions (ordered within \u2264600 time units), we cannot verify a time-respecting chain \u2014 therefore the result is insufficient.\"\n}", "total_input_tokens": 99169, "total_output_tokens": 6809, "total_tokens": 105978, "total_latency_ms": 97597, "llm_calls": 17, "schema_repairs": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}